{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Day 22 — Advanced pandas: apply vs vectorization, query/eval, categoricals\n","Objectives:\n","- Replace apply with vectorized ops where possible.\n","- Use query/eval for performance.\n","- Use Categorical dtype to reduce memory."]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[],"source":["import pandas as pd, numpy as np, seaborn as sns\n","df = sns.load_dataset('tips')\n","# Vectorized tip %\n","df['tip_pct'] = df['tip']/df['total_bill']\n","# Categoricals\n","df['day'] = df['day'].astype('category')\n","df.dtypes\n","# query/eval\n","df.query('tip_pct > 0.2 and size >= 3').head()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Exercises\n","1) Identify a slow apply and replace with vectorized logic.\n","2) Convert high-cardinality string column to category and profile memory.\n"]}]}
